fields.value:
{{Rootnotes
| name = Echo Stomp
| desc = {{Symbol|bonus shd}} [[Root]] sources disables the {{M|Alt-Cast}} {{M|teleport}} component.
}}

 * {{Symbol|Target|Area-Inter}}
** Multiple overlapping Echo Stomp radius fully stack, with each applying its own ability components.
** All ability effects are applied centered around both {{hi|Elder Titan}} the Titan and {{Symbol|Astral Spirit}} the Spirit.

* The ability effects are applied as follows:
*# {{Symbol|Affect|Self}} {{Symbol|Channeling}}
*#* Applies the following ability effects on self while [[channeling]]:
*#** {{M|Root}}
*#* {{Symbol|Channeling|f}}
*#** Interrupting the channeling causes the ability to do nothing, consumes {{M|mana}} and goes into {{M|cooldown}}.
*# {{Symbol|Channeling|t}} {{Symbol|Affect|Self}} {{Symbol|Teleport}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Astral Spirit}}
*#* {{cf|shdnotes}} With {{M|Alt-Cast}} activated, enables [[teleport]]ing the Titan to the Spirit's current location upon a successful [[channeling]].
*#** This immediately reunites both the Titan and the Spirit.
*#** Requires {{U|Astral Spirit}} to be summoned for the teleport component to happen.
*#** Does not {{M|disjoint}} incoming {{M|projectiles}} for the Titan
*# {{Symbol|Channeling|t}}
*#* The {{M|physical}} {{M|spell damage}}.
*# {{Symbol|Channeling|t}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|elder_titan_echo_stomp}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
*#* The debuff applies the following two components at the same time:
*#** [[File:Dota2 Condition-1.png|1|21px]]
*#*** Applies a {{#var:Echo Stomp value4}}-second {{M|stun}} duration, debuff-affected enemy units cannot be awaken while this component is active.
*#*** {{M|Sleep}}
*#**** Affected units are never automatically attacked.
*#**** {{M|Disarm}}
*#** [[File:Dota2 Condition-2.png|2|21px]] {{Symbol|a|Counter}}
*#*** {{#var:Echo Stomp value4}} seconds later, the wake-up damage counter on each debuff-affected enemy unit turns active.
*#*** {{M|Dispels}} the debuff on each affected enemy unit upon accumulating {{Code|w}} damage ([[after reductions]]).
*#**** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|w {{=}} {{#var:Echo Stomp type1 value1}} + {{ValueColor||{{Show|T|Elder Titan|v2r}}|tal|x}}}}
*#***** {{Code|w}} does not consider the {{A|Elder Titan|Astral Spirit}} {{Symbol|Damage|Magical}} {{Symbol|Damage|Physical}} {{M|spell damage}} instance.
*#***** The debuff-affected enemy unit may wake up immediately on the next damage instance when collectively taking a single damage instance {{Code|≥ w}} damage.
*#***** {{cf|talnotes}}
*#****** Learning the {{ValueColor||wake-up damage threshold|10tal}} {{M|talent|t=t1l}} does not update the current {{Code|w}} value.
*#****** However, the talent immediately updates the value of {{Code|w}} while {{M|channeling}} Echo Stomp.
*# {{Symbol|Channeling|t}}
*#* The {{M|magical}} {{M|spell damage}}.

* {{Symbol|Astral Spirit}}
** The Spirit's {{A|Astral Spirit|Echo Stomp}} has the following properties:
*** The ability values are not affected by mechanics applied on the Titan.
*** {{M|Disable}} sources on the Spirit, if applicable, do not affect the Spirit's simutaneous and syncronized ability cast with the Titan.
*** {{Symbol|Channeling}}
**** Applies the following ability effects on the Spirit while [[channeling]]:
***** {{M|Root}}
***** {{M|Cannot Act}}.
****** Hence, stop commands do nothing while the Titan is channeling.
*** {{Symbol|bonus cd}}
**** The Spirit's ability cast does nothing and goes on [[cooldown]], while the Titan is affected by {{M|disable}} sources.

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Echo Stomp icon0}}
| desc = CHANNELED - Elder Titan and his Astral Spirit both stomp the ground, damaging and knocking nearby enemy units unconscious around their locations.  The Elder Titan stomp deals physical damage, while the Spirit stomp deals magical damage.
}}
* {{cf|shdnotes}} {{M|Alt-Cast}} is disabled by default upon acquiring the {{M|Aghanim's Shard|text=ability upgrade}}.

